# Failure 3 — loader_app: URI with undefined scheme (DAG run 21:19)

MIG_TARGET_SYSTEM_URL had been set with 'gcloud composer environments update'. Terraform owns
config.softwareConfig.envVariables, so a later apply reverted it and the loader was
handed an empty target URL. The failure surfaced three DAG runs after the change that
caused it — which is the argument for the config living in IaC rather than in a
convenience command.

## Captured from Cloud Logging
```
[base] Exception in thread "main" java.lang.IllegalArgumentException: URI with undefined scheme
[base] 	at ro.mig.loader.LoaderApp.main(LoaderApp.java:100)
[base] 	at ro.mig.loader.LoaderApp$Loader.push(LoaderApp.java:196)
[base] 	at ro.mig.loader.LoaderApp$Loader.send(LoaderApp.java:223)
[base] 	at java.net.http/java.net.http.HttpRequest.newBuilder(Unknown Source)
```

## Fix
terraform/modules/composer declares MIG_TARGET_SYSTEM_URL, MIG_JAVA_IMAGE_TAG, KAFKA_BOOTSTRAP,
DATAFLOW_SUBNETWORK and DATAFLOW_SERVICE_ACCOUNT; envs/dev passes the real values.
A new java_image_tag variable carries the tag build_java_images.sh printed.
